"blend_materials": "Shared exposed-neighbour colours join rock, soil and turf over the same lattice edges, including chunk boundaries and digging.",
"scree_density": "A 0.09 total base density, divided across three irregular slab variants, leaves ground largely clear; fragments are non-harvestable.",
"scree_width": "24-centimetre fragments stay visually smaller than harvestable boulders.",
"scree_height": "5.5-centimetre fragments sit partly buried, with broad tops instead of pointed pyramid shapes.",
"surface_contrast": "Historical shader setting; the v3 shader uses soil_exposure, stone_moss and its apparent-relief fields instead.",
"strata_metres": "Historical shader setting; v3 uses continuous broken mineral bedding with rock_bump_m controlling its apparent relief.",
"grain_metres": "Size of the fine soil/stone grain, filtered out before it can shimmer at distance.",
"linear_vertex_colours": "Convert authored sRGB cover colours to the linear values consumed by the foliage shader.",
"cover_tint": "Earthier vegetation reduces pale green highlights without changing threat VFX.",
"detail_distance": "Fade small boulders and mineral ribbons beyond 65 metres, preserving nearby harvesting reads.",
"tree_distance": "Keep tree silhouettes visible to 200 metres while limiting distant prop submissions.",
"cover_distance": "Keep grass and reeds within 55 metres; their chunk batches fade over an eight-metre margin.",
"seam_steps": "24 short spans across a three-metre mineral ribbon let it follow sloping terrain.",
"seam_half_width": "A 0.24-metre half-width keeps fractures readable without looking like roads.",
"seam_surface_lift": "Lift the ribbon 0.018 metres above sampled terrain to avoid coplanar flicker.",
"soft_terrain": "Shared occupancy normals soften the tiny triangle lighting while leaving collision and editable voxels unchanged.",
"turf_slope_start": "Historical unblended materials: upward normal where slope-based turf begins; shared-colour terrain uses actual neighbouring materials instead.",
"turf_slope_end": "Historical unblended materials: upward normal where slope-based turf becomes complete.",
"top_colours": "Owner revision, 5 Sep: earthier olive turf and weathered slate; marsh and strata retain their identity.",
"side_colours": "Exposed soil beneath turf makes elevation readable without coating every vertical step in grass.",
"patch_metres": "Broad twenty-one-metre weathering patches relate the close material grain to the continuous landscape.",
"detail_metres": "Historical shader setting; v3 uses grain_metres and continuous world-space weathering for close detail.",
"colour_variation": "Quiet large moss, loam and dry-turf patches break the flat carpet while resources and threats keep stronger accents.",
"grass_edge_depth": "How far turf hangs down the top of an exposed soil edge, as a fraction of a block.",
"cover_patch_metres": "Size of the sparse and lush ground-cover patches; does not move trees or resources.",
